--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. THE FALSE NEGATIVE THIS RUN ALMOST REPORTED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The bottleneck is a THREE-STAGE core-to-core pipeline: conv2dk1 (1x1), conv2dk3 (3x3), and
conv2dk1_skip (1x1 + skip). conv2dk1_skip.cc carries the SAME array-accumulator defect, on its
own two reduction loops.

Patching only conv2dk1.cc -- which is what "fix the 1x1 conv's accumulator residency" literally
asks for -- and measuring at 32x32, iters=10, three runs in one sitting:

STOCK
      HxW     MFLOP   wall ms     hw ms   host ms   hw GOPS  e2e GOPS  ok
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    32x32    142.61    2.2220    1.4844    0.7375      96.1      64.2  yes

not enough verified shapes to fit

conv2dk1.cc ONLY
      HxW     MFLOP   wall ms     hw ms   host ms   hw GOPS  e2e GOPS  ok
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    32x32    142.61    2.1780    1.4486    0.7294      98.4      65.5  yes

not enough verified shapes to fit

BOTH 1x1 STAGES
      HxW     MFLOP   wall ms     hw ms   host ms   hw GOPS  e2e GOPS  ok
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    32x32    142.61    1.2398    0.6133    0.6265     232.5     115.0  yes

not enough verified shapes to fit

Read alone, the middle table is a null result -- 1.4844 -> 1.4486 ms, 2.4%, inside this
machine's own drift -- and it would have been reported as one: "the conv is delivery-bound
too, like the GEMM." It is instead Amdahl. A pipeline runs at the rate of its slowest stage,
and stage 3 still had its accumulators in memory. Fixing both takes the same shape to
0.6133 ms, 2.42x.

The lesson is not about this kernel. It is that a single-stage intervention in a multi-stage
pipeline measures the pipeline's balance, not the intervention.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. STATIC -- what the compiler did, no hardware involved
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
tools/aie_disasm.py on the objects each arm actually compiled.

conv2dk1_i8_vector, the hot reduction loop:

                                   stock              patched
  bundles in the loop                 22                   14
  vmac in the loop                     1                    4
  MAC issue rate              0.045/cyc            0.286/cyc     6.29x
  accumulator quarter loads            4                    0
  accumulator quarter stores           4                    0
  bundles issuing nothing              6                    3
  slot density                 0.91 of 6            1.00 of 6
  acc registers named          3 (cm0-cm2)          5 (cm0-cm4)

The stock loop, verbatim -- four vlda of amhh1/amhl1/amlh1/amll1 in, one vmac, four vst of
amhh2/amhl2/amlh2/amll2 out, six dead bundles:

        vlda	amhh1, [p3, #0x60]
        vlda	amhl1, [p3, #0x40] | vldb	wl2, [p7, dj1]
        vlda	amlh1, [p3, #0x20]
        vlda	amll1, [p3, #0x0]
        (all nop) x2
        vmac	cm2, cm1, x2, x0, r30
        (all nop) x4
        vst	amhh2, [p3, #0x60]
        vst	amhl2, [p3, #0x40]
        vst	amlh2, [p3, #0x20] | add	r29, r29, #0x1
        vst	amll2, [p3, #0x0]  | add	r28, r28, #0x20

and the patched loop -- no accumulator traffic at all, four vmac on named cm1-cm4:

        vlda	wh8, [p7, #0x20] | paddb	[p3], m2
        vlda	wl8, [p7], #0x40 | vldb	wl6, [p3], #0x20
        vldb	wl4, [p3], #0x20
        vldb	wl2, [p3, #0x0]
        vldb	wl0, [p3, #0x20]
        (all nop) x3
        vmac	cm4, cm4, x6, x8, r10
        vmac	cm3, cm3, x4, x8, r10
        vmac	cm2, cm2, x2, x8, r10
        add	r24, r24, r12 | vmac	cm1, cm1, x0, x8, r10

conv2dk1_skip_i8_vector has two reduction halves and both moved the same way: two 22-bundle
loops at density 0.91 become two 14-bundle loops at density 1.00, with 6 accumulator registers
named instead of 5.

Both functions grew in total size (163 -> 215 bundles, 218 -> 359) because the peel is an added
fast path and the array loop is kept as the tail. Stack frame is unchanged at 768 B in both --
this fix moves the ACCUMULATORS into registers; it does not empty the frame the way H11 did on
the GEMM.

