3. A/B ON HARDWARE -- alternating arms, each with its own NPU_CACHE_HOME
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The cache home is per-arm and the driver requires it: @iron.jit keys its cache on the
design and its compile-time arguments, NOT on the kernel source, so a patched build with
the same arguments would silently reuse the stock arm's whole xclbin. That is not
hypothetical -- it happened to the reblocked GEMM in this repo, and the only symptom was
that no new .o appeared on disk. Verified here by grepping the peel out of the source
copy the compiler actually consumed.

